# Config Drift Governance — environment configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and adjust as needed, OR set these as
# real environment variables. NEVER commit a real .env with secrets.
#
# Everything below is OPTIONAL. With no .env at all, the backend auto-detects the
# workspace root (this folder) and reads/writes:
#     Config report/   (inputs + generated CSVs)
#     UIUX/assets/     (generated *.js for the frontend)
# so the offline build works out of the box after `pip install -r requirements.txt`.

# --- Workspace root ----------------------------------------------------------
# Leave BLANK to auto-detect (recommended). Set only if you keep the data folder
# ("Config report/") somewhere other than this package.
WHS_WORKSPACE=

# --- Neo4j (only for build_graph.py and the other *_graph.py builders) -------
# The static frontend uses the shipped snapshot (UIUX/assets/graph-snapshot.js),
# so you do NOT need Neo4j just to view the UI.
NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
NEO4J_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=

# --- OPTIONAL live connectors (not needed for the offline build) -------------
# Power BI (pbi_drift_alert.py) — pull drift straight from the dataset instead
# of the shipped data.xlsx:
# PBI_DATASET_ID=
# PBI_GROUP_ID=
# PBI_TENANT_ID=
# PBI_CLIENT_ID=

# SharePoint (sharepoint_reader.py) — sign-in hint for MSAL device/interactive:
# SP_LOGIN_HINT=you@pg.com

# SQL replica connector (validate_against_replica.py) — path to Diamond's db.py
# (external, not shipped in this package):
# DIAMOND_DB_PATH=
